    "section_faq_bmpaKY": {
      "type": "section-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "text_qLCUnV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Should I wash my Waterproof Mattress Protector before first use?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>We know that when you’re travelling, a pre-wash isn’t always practical. It’s absolutely fine to put your new protector straight onto the bed and start using it.</p><p>Simply wash it as part of your regular bedding routine when it suits you.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "text_r4rfmd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "How should I wash my Waterproof Mattress Protector?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Machine wash your Mattress Protector on a regular cold wash cycle using a mild detergent.</p><p>Because of its waterproof properties, the protector can hold a significant amount of water during washing. We recommend using a washing machine with a drum large enough for the protector to move freely and, where possible, a high-speed spin cycle to help remove excess water before drying.</p><p>Avoid overloading your washing machine and make sure the protector has plenty of room to move freely within the drum.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "text_T7fhDz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can I use bleach or fabric softener?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>No. We recommend avoiding bleach and fabric softeners, as harsh laundry products can damage the waterproof membrane and reduce the performance and lifespan of your Mattress Protector.</p><p>A mild laundry detergent is all you need to keep it fresh and clean.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "text_8QTRXM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "How should I dry my Waterproof Mattress Protector?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Your Mattress Protector can be line dried or tumble dried on a low heat setting.</p><p>Because the waterproof backing can retain water during washing, a high-speed spin before drying will help remove excess moisture and reduce drying time.</p><p>Make sure the protector is completely dry before placing it back on your bed or storing it.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "text_KePhEm": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can I iron or dry clean my Waterproof Mattress Protector?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>No. Your Dreamer RV Waterproof Mattress Protector should not be ironed or dry cleaned, as these processes can damage the materials and waterproof backing.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "text_WBcdai": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "How often should I wash my Mattress Protector?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Your Mattress Protector doesn’t necessarily need to be washed every time you wash your sheets.</p><p>As a general guide, many customers wash their Mattress Protector every few sheet changes, or more often if needed.</p><p>We also recommend washing it promptly after any spills or accidents to help keep your sleep setup fresh, clean and protected.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "text_Kjq6iC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Is the entire Mattress Protector waterproof?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>The sleep surface of the Mattress Protector is waterproof, helping protect the mattress and topper underneath from spills and accidents.</p><p>The fitted side panels are designed to stretch around your bed and are not waterproof, so liquids that come into contact with the sides may still reach the mattress or topper underneath.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        }
      },
